  "name": "Baseline - Windows - Device Guard / Credential Guard / HVCI",
  "description": "Virtualisation-based security: Credential Guard, HVCI (memory integrity) and Secure Boot enforcement, enabled without UEFI lock so it remains remotely reversible. Requires compatible hardware and can break old kernel-mode drivers, so pilot before broad rollout. Pairs with the virtualizationBasedSecurityEnabled and memoryIntegrityEnabled checks in the Windows compliance policy. Derived from OpenIntuneBaseline.",
